[
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Shall there be an amendment to the Colorado Constitution concerning congressional redistricting, and, in connection therewith, reenacting the current process for congressional redistricting in the Colorado Constitution and prohibiting modifications to a final map unless at least three public meetings are held, the modifications do not have the effect of dividing communities of interest or purposefully favoring one political party, and are approved by the congressional redistricting commission and the Colorado Supreme Court?",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Who put the measure on the ballot?",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-heading",
    "version": 1,
    "tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Amendment 86 was placed on the ballot through a citizen initiative backed by operatives of ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Advance Colorado",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://whoisadvancecolorado.com/"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": ", a right-wing group supporting numerous measures on Colorado’s 2026 ballot.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Short Description:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-heading",
    "version": 1,
    "tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Reenacts the current congressional redistricting process in the Colorado Constitution and imposes requirements on any off-cycle redistricting: a modified map would require at least three public meetings, could not purposefully favor a political party or divide communities of interest, and would need approval by the independent congressional redistricting commission and the Colorado Supreme Court.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Analysis and Commentary:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-heading",
    "version": 1,
    "tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Oppose. Amendment 86 was placed on the ballot through a citizen initiative backed by operatives of ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Advance Colorado",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://whoisadvancecolorado.com/"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": ", a right-wing group supporting numerous measures on Colorado’s 2026 ballot.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "In 2018, Colorado voters passed Amendments X and Y, which set up requirements for the state’s redistricting of US House seats and all state legislature seats, requiring an independent / cross-partisan commission. That process takes place every ten years after the U.S. Decennial Census.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "I supported those measures in 2018, and still believe the process is a good one for Colorado, particularly for our state legislature. Gerrymandering of representative seats leads to terrible power dynamics, bad incentives for legislators and districts, and is bad for democracy. ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "However, Republicans nationally, and conservatives on the United States Supreme Court, have broken that contract with voters at the federal level, which is why Colorado needs flexibility to manage its redistricting system. Look no further than mid-cycle redistricting efforts by Republican-led states of Florida, North Carolina, Ohio, Tennessee, Texas all attempted or enacted efforts to ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "increase Republican gerrymanders",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://ballotpedia.org/Redistricting_ahead_of_the_2026_elections"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": " mid-cycle between 2024 and 2026. That’s on top of the conservative Supreme Court completing their ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "dismantling of the Voting Rights Act",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://afj.org/article/the-supreme-courts-overturning-of-the-voting-rights-act-is-complete/"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": " which has continued to enable more partisan and racial gerrymanders. In many ways, Colorado passing Amendment Y for congressional redistricting was preemptive disarmament in a war that Republicans intend to wage until the end.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Conversely in 2021, US House Democrats passed ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "HR1: For the People Act of 2021",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/1"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": ". Among other national voter protections, the bill would have required that “states to establish independent redistricting commissions to carry out congressional redistricting,” like the system that Colorado has independently approved. However, rather famously, the bill was ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "opposed by Senate Democrats Joe Manchin and Kyrsten Sinema",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/07/joe-manchin-voting-rights-bill-democrats-splits"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": ", and failed to become law.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Until we can get rid of partisan and racial gerrymandering at the federal level, Colorado should not continue to put impediments toward our state having a level playing field. That’s why I’m voting no on Amendment 86.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
